// expect: refuse E_TypeMismatch
// A DEFAULT'S CALL IS NOT A CALL EDGE. `y = helper(1)` makes `y` a String,
// so `x + y` is a type error. The program checks clean (measured
// 2026-09-25): the free-name walk never enters parameter defaults, so `f`
// has no edge to `helper` and is judged before `helper` is. Declaring
// `helper` first refuses it, which is the right verdict in both orders.
//
// Retires when the call graph is read from resolved references, the
// default's included (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge).
fn f(x, y = helper(1)) = x + y

fn helper(n) = "s"

fn main() = f(1)
